                <pb facs="0232" n="225" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg225"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/8827: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-20T18:00:00-04:00">July 20, 1947—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>130. Your 258, July 19, 3 p.m., and 256, July 18, 3 p.m., paragraph 3. Department
                    continues to hold the view expressed in its 116, July 13, 7 p.m.</p>
                <pb facs="0233" n="226" xml:id="pg226"/>
                <p>On July 18 the Chinese Ambassador here, in response to an oral inquiry, expressed
                    personal opinion that it was preferable that you remain at Peiping.</p>
                <p>Please continue to keep the Department informed of developments and of your views
                    in this regard.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
